From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 09:59:54 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] wuapi: scriptable Windows Update Agent objects, an empty
 search, collections (3006)

The session, searcher, downloader, installer, automatic updates and system
information objects implemented only IUnknown: IDispatch answered E_NOTIMPL, so
no script could use them. They now answer through the type library
(dispatch.c), keep their properties (ClientApplicationID, IsForced, Priority,
Online, ServerSelection, ServiceID, AllowSourcePrompts, ParentHwnd/ParentWindow,
Updates, ...) and the searcher works the way a system whose updates come from its
package manager would: Search finds nothing (ISearchResult succeeded, with empty
Updates, RootCategories and Warnings), QueryHistory and GetTotalHistoryCount are
empty, EscapeString doubles single quotes. The collections are real
(collection.c): IStringCollection and IUpdateCollection are read-write lists with
Add, Insert, RemoveAt, Clear, Copy and enumerators; category, exception and
history collections are empty. AutomaticUpdates reports no service and its
DetectNow, Pause and Resume succeed. wuapi imports oleaut32 for the BSTRs.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
